Usage: agent-deck recall timeline <session> --json [--since <cursor> | --before <cursor> --limit N] [--limit N] [--tail N] [--agent <id>] [--kinds a,b] [--skip-empty-body]
       agent-deck recall timeline --json --transcript <file> --harness claude|codex|pi
       agent-deck recall timeline --json [--tail N] [--kinds a,b] [--skip-empty-body] --sessions <id1>,<id2>,...   (batch: one entry per id, at most 50)
       agent-deck recall timeline <session> --json --v1   (slice-6 turn shape)
<session>: deck session id, title or id prefix; a Claude, Codex or Pi conversation id; or #n / any id the index knows.
Rows are parsed from the native transcript directly, whatever the index or its deferral state. Needs [recall] enabled = true.
With --kinds or --skip-empty-body, --tail and --limit count kept rows. A native read then carries next_cursor: pass it to --since (never a cursor made from the last kept row). --agent sidechains and index-backed rows have no cursor.
  -agent string
    	One Claude Code sub-agent sidechain by agent id
  -before string
    	Return older rows before this before_cursor (requires --limit N)
  -harness string
    	With --transcript: claude, codex or pi
  -json
    	Output canonical JSON
  -kinds string
    	Comma-separated row kinds to keep (user, assistant, thinking, tool, bash, edit, read, subagent, todo, question, skill, command, system, compaction, turn_end, other); filtered here, before output, sub-agent children included. Native reads other than --agent resume with next_cursor
  -limit int
    	Maximum older rows with --before; otherwise stop after N new rows and resume with --since
  -sessions string
    	Comma-separated session ids: one call answers each id's timeline (at most 50; only --tail, --kinds and --skip-empty-body combine with it)
  -since string
    	Only what changed after this cursor: new rows in turns, changes to earlier rows in updates/removed
  -skip-empty-body
    	Drop rows whose body is empty or only whitespace (a tool call still waiting for its result is kept); filtered here, before output, sub-agent children included. Native reads other than --agent resume with next_cursor
  -tail int
    	Only the last N rows, read from the end of the transcript (fast first paint)
  -transcript string
    	Read this Claude Code JSONL, Codex rollout or Pi session instead of a session's
  -v1
    	Slice-6 output (turns with role/kind/text, turn frames) instead of rows
